From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:10:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: udc: return the error of a remote wakeup from
 srp

Writing 1 to the UDC's srp attribute asks the controller to wake the
host, but the result of usb_gadget_wakeup() is dropped, so the write
succeeds even when the controller refuses (the bus isn't suspended, or
the host didn't enable remote wakeup) or can't wake the host at all.

Return the error, so userspace can tell.

Signed-off-by: Chris Blake <chrisrblake93@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c
index f6da12b55..8dae38d5a 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/udc/core.c
@@ -1792,9 +1792,13 @@ static ssize_t srp_store(struct device *dev,
 		struct device_attribute *attr, const char *buf, size_t n)
 {
 	struct usb_udc		*udc = container_of(dev, struct usb_udc, dev);
+	int			ret;
 
-	if (sysfs_streq(buf, "1"))
-		usb_gadget_wakeup(udc->gadget);
+	if (sysfs_streq(buf, "1")) {
+		ret = usb_gadget_wakeup(udc->gadget);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
 
 	return n;
 }
